# Names that must resolve to a container instead of to the real internet.
# Consulted by the catch-all block of the Corefile, with fallthrough, so
# anything not listed here is forwarded upstream as usual.
#
# Empty on purpose, and kept rather than deleted: the Corefile's catch-all
# block consults it, and this is where a name that must resolve to a container
# and CANNOT be a Docker network alias would go.
#
# The dev hostnames — acme-console.localhost, acme-api.localhost,
# acme-challenge.localhost, keycloak.localhost — are not here. They are
# network aliases on the traefik service in compose.yaml, which Docker's own
# embedded resolver answers before anything reaches CoreDNS. keycloak.localhost
# in particular is load-bearing rather than merely convenient: it is the OIDC
# issuer host, and the issuer has to be ONE URL that resolves from the browser
# on the host and from inside the api container alike, because go-oidc
# requires the issuer it discovers to match the one it was configured with.
